IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- PART 10A, TRANSFER OF REGISTRATION: s 360 (when registration must be refused), lines 23335 to 23360 of CoA1967.txt.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sge)"). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- The Registrar's satisfaction is a judgment the text hands to the Registrar: each is a conditional input ("if the Registrar is satisfied that ..."),
-- never guessed. The "minimum requirements prescribed" are the regulations' (s 364A(a)), so the person says whether they have been met.

DECLARE `s 360 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 360(1) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
    `s 360(2) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
    `s 360(3) appeal to the Minister`

§ `Section 360(1): refusal for want of the requirements`

-- "The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if the Registrar is not satisfied that the minimum requirements prescribed
-- for registration have been met and that all other requirements for registration have been complied with."
-- Read as: not satisfied of both. A failed "if" is read as the text's no (the reading (a) left to a lawyer; NOTES.md, Marginal readings).
-- src:23337 | 360.—(1) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate
-- src:23338 | entity if the Registrar is not satisfied that the minimum requirements
-- src:23339 | prescribed for registration have been met and that all other
-- src:23340 | requirements for registration have been complied with.
@ref s 360(1) (src:23337-23340)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the minimum requirements prescribed for registration have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that all other requirements for registration have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the minimum requirements prescribed for registration have been met`
      AND `the Registrar is satisfied that all other requirements for registration have been complied with`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must refuse ... if the Registrar is not satisfied that ..." (a failed "if" read as the text's no, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29: marginal reading for a lawyer; fork line F-360-1 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:23337 | 360.—(1) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate
-- src:23338 | entity if the Registrar is not satisfied that the minimum requirements
-- src:23339 | prescribed for registration have been met and that all other
-- src:23340 | requirements for registration have been complied with.
@ref s 360(1) (src:23337-23340)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 360 act`
`s 360(1) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if not satisfied that the requirements have been met` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 360(1) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 360(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not refuse to register a foreign corporate entity that the Registrar was not satisfied had met the requirements for registration" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 360(2): refusal on public grounds`

-- (a) "the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore".
-- src:23344 | (2) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if
-- src:23345 | the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:23347 | (a) the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful
-- src:23348 | purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare
-- src:23349 | or good order in Singapore; or
@ref s 360(2)(a) (src:23344-23349)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(2)(a) the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for a purpose that the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph is one of two grounds joined by "or"; that the Registrar is not satisfied of this one says nothing about the other

-- (b) "it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered".
-- src:23344 | (2) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if
-- src:23345 | the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:23351 | (b) it would be contrary to national security or interest for the
-- src:23352 | intended company to be registered.
@ref s 360(2)(b) (src:23344-23352)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(2)(b) the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph is one of two grounds joined by "or"; that the Registrar is not satisfied of this one says nothing about the other

-- "The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if the Registrar is satisfied that — (a) ...; or (b) ...".
-- src:23344 | (2) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if
-- src:23345 | the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:23347 | (a) the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful
-- src:23348 | purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare
-- src:23349 | or good order in Singapore; or
-- src:23351 | (b) it would be contrary to national security or interest for the
-- src:23352 | intended company to be registered.
@ref s 360(2) (src:23344-23352)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` MEANS
    IF    `s 360(2)(a) the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for a purpose that the paragraph names` `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose` `the Registrar is satisfied that the intended company is likely to be used for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 360(2)(b) the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to national security or interest for the intended company to be registered` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must refuse ... if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) ...; or (b) ...": with neither ground made out the subsection requires no refusal (a failed "if" read as the text's no, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29: marginal reading for a lawyer; fork line F-360-2 in NOTES.md)

-- src:23344 | (2) The Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if
-- src:23345 | the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:23347 | (a) the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful
-- src:23348 | purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare
-- src:23349 | or good order in Singapore; or
-- src:23351 | (b) it would be contrary to national security or interest for the
-- src:23352 | intended company to be registered.
@ref s 360(2) (src:23344-23352)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 360 act`
`s 360(2) the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign corporate entity if satisfied of a ground in the subsection` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 360(2) refuse to register the foreign corporate entity`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 360(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not refuse to register a foreign corporate entity although satisfied of a ground in section 360(2)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 360(3): appeal to the Minister`

-- "Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (1) or (2) may, within 30 days after the date of the decision,
-- appeal to the Minister whose decision is final."
-- src:23356 | (3) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:23357 | subsection (1) or (2) may, within 30 days after the date of the
-- src:23358 | decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 360(3) (src:23356-23358)
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is the decision of the Registrar under section 360(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the date the appeal is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(3) the person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is aggrieved by the decision`) OR (NOT `the decision is the decision of the Registrar under section 360(1) or (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to "Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under subsection (1) or (2)"; for anyone else, or another decision, the text grants nothing and says nothing (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-360-3 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is within a period after` `the date of the decision` `the date the appeal is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days after the date of the decision, appeal" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

-- src:23358 | decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 360(3) (src:23358-23358)
GIVEN `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 360(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 360(3) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Minister's decision on an appeal under section 360(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "appeal to the Minister whose decision is final" speaks of the Minister's decision on this appeal only

-- The appeal as a permission with a window of 30 days after the decision (AT 0 is the day of the decision). A permission cannot be breached.
-- src:23356 | (3) Any person aggrieved by the decision of the Registrar under
-- src:23357 | subsection (1) or (2) may, within 30 days after the date of the
-- src:23358 | decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 360(3) (src:23356-23358)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 360 act`
`s 360(3) a person aggrieved may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MAY `s 360(3) appeal to the Minister`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
